  "annotations": {},
  "appreciation": "Nalan Xingde wrote this while travelling with the imperial escort beyond the pass, and the poem moves to the rhythm of the march. Mountains, rivers, wind and snow accumulate in parallel phrases until the noise of the storm breaks the dream that would have carried him home. Its plain language makes the homesickness feel immediate rather than literary.",
